[31.164739, "o", "\u001b[?25l\r\n\r\n \u001b[1m←\u001b[m open sidebar · Interactive · Allow All · \u001b[1m/\u001b[m commands · \u001b[1m?\u001b[m help · \u001b[1mtab\u001b[m next tab\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[31.220406, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\n\r\n   • The command line contains \u001b[37m MiniDump \u001b[m or \u001b[37m #24 \u001b[m.\u001b[56C \u001b[B\u001b[1K\r\n   The rule runs on the Endpoint.Processes data model, so it depends on process-creation events (Sysmon EID \r\n   1) being mapped into that data model.\u001b[67C \u001b[B\u001b[1K ┃\r\r\n   \u001b[1mWhat it would miss:\u001b[m                       \u001b[62C  ┃\r\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K ┃\r\r\n   • \u001b[1mOther binaries:\u001b[m a copied or renamed rundll32 is only caught if \u001b[37m original_file_name \u001b[m is still intact. A  ┃\r\r\n\u001b[5Cdifferent loader of comsvcs, or a rundll32 whose original filename is stripped, is missed.\u001b[14C┃\r\r\n   • \u001b[1mOrdinal variants:\u001b[m \u001b[37m #+24 \u001b[m, \u001b[37m #0024 \u001b[m or \u001b[37m #024 \u001b[m. The rule matches only the literal \u001b[37m #24 \u001b[m.        \u001b[5C      ┃\r\r\n   • \u001b[1mObfuscation:\u001b[m                                                                                   \u001b[9C┃\r\r\n\u001b[5C• Caret escapes, such as \u001b[37m Mini^Dump \u001b[m.\u001b[67C┃\r\r\n     • Split or concatenated strings.\u001b[72C┃\r\r\n\u001b[5C• A comsvcs.dll path built fro"]
[31.220414, "o", "m environment variables.\u001b[50C┃\r\r\n     • Command lines that are wrapped or encoded, for example through PowerShell or cmd.                     ┃\r\r\n   • \u001b[1mNot process-based:\u001b[m a dump made from LSASS access by something other than rundll32 would only be caught  ┃\r\r\n     by the Sysmon EID 10 rules, and those are disabled.\u001b[53C┃\r\r\n   • \u001b[1mFilter macro:\u001b[m \u001b[37m dump_lsass_via_comsvcs_dll_filter \u001b[m is the default \u001b[37m search * \u001b[m, so there are no\r\n     exclusions.                                                                                            \r\n\r\n   I haven't tested these variants against the attack data. I changed nothing.\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mNext step:\u001b[m I can build a Sigma-based detection in \u001b[37m acme-detections \u001b[m, with crafted variant tests, if you\r\n   want one. The alternative is to ask for the ESCU rule to be enabled.                                     \u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
