[121.751482, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[3;4H\u001b[90m├\u001b[3;31H┼\u001b[3;40H┼\u001b[3;49H┤\u001b[m                                                  \r\n   \u001b[90m│\u001b[m Real MiniDump\u001b[4;31H\u001b[90m│\u001b[m fires  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m fires  \u001b[90m│\r\n\u001b[3C├──────────────────────────┼────────┼────────┤\u001b[m                                                          \r\n   \u001b[90m│\u001b[m #+24                     \u001b[90m│\u001b[m silent \u001b[90m│\u001b[m fires  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m                                                    \r\n   \u001b[90m├──────────────────────────┼────────┼────────┤\r\n\u001b[3C│\u001b[m #65560\u001b[8;31H\u001b[90m│\u001b[m silent \u001b[90m│\u001b[m fires  \u001b[90m│\r\n\u001b[3C├──────────────────────────┼────────┼────────┤\u001b[m                                                         \r\n   \u001b[90m│\u001b[m #-65512                  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m silent \u001b[90m"]
[121.751497, "o", "│\u001b[m fires  \u001b[90m│\u001b[m                              \r\n   \u001b[90m├──────────────────────────┼────────┼────────┤\r\n\u001b[3C│\u001b[m Benign RegisterComponent \u001b[90m│\u001b[m silent \u001b[90m│\u001b[m silent \u001b[90m│\u001b[m                                                        \r\n   \u001b[90m└──────────────────────────┴────────┴────────┘\u001b[m                                        \r\n\r\n   So ESCU misses the three ordinal variants and our detection catches them.\r\n\r\n   \u001b[1mNoise and AI triage:\u001b[m All 16 alerts come from one account and host, \u001b[37m svc_purpleteam \u001b[m on\u001b[14C     \r\n   \u001b[37m PT-LAB-01.acme.example \u001b[m. Eight are \u001b[37m powershell.exe \u001b[m and eight are \u001b[37m rundll32.exe \u001b[m, the same dump seen at\r\n   both levels of the process chain. The AI Toolkit judged this expected: scheduled purple-team LSASS dumps \r\n   in the lab.                      "]
[121.751522, "o", "                                                                        \u001b[B\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mNext step:\u001b[m the AGENTS.md tuning rule applies here. The filter macro would exclude \u001b[37m user=\"svc_purpleteam\" \r\n\u001b[C\u001b[m  \u001b[37mdest=\"PT-LAB-01.acme.example\" \u001b[m together, and the description would record who approved it. It would also \r\n   get a \u001b[37m none \u001b[m test case for that activity. The procdump and mimikatz detections already have the same      ┃\r\r\n   exclusion for CHG-2077. Whether the same approval covers this detection is your call, so tell me and I'll\r\n   add it and rerun CI.                                                                                     \u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
